Specifications
--------------
The model, readers, writers and checks are written from public specifications:
  - ORCID Message Schema v3.0 (https://github.com/ORCID/orcid-model)
  - ORCID iD structure and check digit, ISO/IEC 7064:2003 MOD 11-2
    (https://support.orcid.org/hc/en-us/articles/360006897674)
  - ORCID API documentation for the Public API and OAuth
    (https://info.orcid.org/documentation/)
  - XML 1.0 (Fifth Edition), W3C Recommendation
No code was copied from other ORCID software (COMPARISON.md, "Shared code").

Third-party material in this repository
---------------------------------------
None of it is in the published crate (Cargo.toml `include`); it is used by
the tests only.

reference/orcid-model/
  The ORCID message schema v3.0 (XSDs, README and samples for record_3.0 and
  group-id-3.0, and common_3.0), copied unmodified from https://github.com/ORCID/orcid-model at
  commit 9592e2d3bde21a1edf703f26f8bc304448f886fb.
  Copyright © 2012-2018 ORCID, Inc. ORCID MIT-style license:
  reference/orcid-model/LICENSE. Provenance: reference/orcid-model/PROVENANCE.md.

Test data
---------
tests/data/0000-0003-0100-6634.xml is the public ORCID record of
0000-0003-0100-6634 as returned by https://pub.orcid.org/v3.0/. ORCID makes
public record data available under CC0 1.0
(https://info.orcid.org/documentation/integration-guide/orcid-public-data-file/).

tests/data/0000-0002-2771-9344.xml is the public ORCID record of
0000-0002-2771-9344 (a fictitious person's record that ORCID uses as an
example), as returned by https://pub.orcid.org/v3.0/0000-0002-2771-9344/record,
unmodified; CC0 1.0 like the record above. The walkthrough and the examples'
usage lines read it.

tests/data/changes/old.xml is the ORCID sample record
reference/orcid-model/record_3.0/samples/read_samples/record-3.0.xml (fictitious
iD 8888-8888-8888-8880); new.xml is an edited copy of it. Both are copied from
yorc-duckdb's test/data/changes, where they were made for its orcid_changes
tests. tests/data/group-id-records.xml is the group-id-records page of
yorc-duckdb's test/sql/orcid_api_messages.test, written for these tests.

tests/data/dump/orcid_test_summaries.tar.gz is a small archive in the layout
of the ORCID Public Data File, copied from yorc-duckdb
(test/data/dump/orcid_test_summaries.tar.gz, byte for byte): the record above,
the ORCID sample records record-3.0.xml and works-3.0.xml (the latter under a
path longer than 100 characters) and a README.txt member. Its contents are
covered by the notices above.

